      "descriptions": [
        {
          "description": "Clinical records of 1,205 pregnant women seen at Kurigram General Hospital, a district hospital in rural northern Bangladesh: age, blood pressure, blood sugar, body temperature, body mass index, heart rate, medical history and a pregnancy risk level (low or high).",
          "descriptionType": "Abstract"
        },
        {
          "description": "Origin: Daffodil International University and Kurigram General Hospital, Mojumdar MU et al. (2025). Maternal health risk factors dataset: clinical parameters and insights from rural Bangladesh. Data in Brief 59: 111363. Taken from the BioBench R package (dataset highriskpreg), which took them from the biostatlab package, which took them from the Mendeley Data file. Column names were turned into snake_case and blank risk levels coded as missing.",
          "descriptionType": "Methods"
        }
